course: dictionary
lesson: 2578
title: Democratic and fair decisions
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Democratic» comes from democracy, a system where people choose their leaders by voting and everyone has equal rights. When something is democratic, it is fair and everyone has an equal say. «We made a democratic decision to name the class pet by a show of hands.» Every child got one hand to vote with, so the decision was fair.
explain: Look at the words around a new word to find its meaning. «Democratic countries hold free elections.» Elections are when people vote for their leaders, so democratic must have something to do with people voting. Try your meaning in the sentence: «Countries based on people voting hold free elections.» That still makes sense, so you have got it.
explain: Capital letters can change the meaning. «The Democratic Republic of the Congo» is the name of a country, so Democratic is part of its name, not a description of fairness. In a sentence like this, ask yourself: is this word describing something, or is it a name?
fact: Democratic means based on democracy, or fair, with everyone having an equal say.
fact: Democracy is a system where people choose their leaders by voting.
fact: «Democratic rights» means rights that everyone has equally.
fact: Ancient Athens is called the birthplace of democracy.
fact: With a capital D, Democratic can mean the Democratic Party in US politics, or be part of a country's name, like «the Democratic Republic of the Congo».
exercise: «a democratic vote in class» What does democratic mean here? | *Fair, with everyone having an equal say | Secret, with one person deciding | Quick and short | Loud and noisy
exercise: «Democratic countries hold free elections.» What does democratic mean in this sentence? | Very old | Rich and powerful | *Based on people voting for their leaders | Having lots of rules
exercise: «The Democratic Republic of the Congo» is a country. Why is Democratic written with a capital D? | It means fair | It means very old | *It is part of a country's name | It is the start of a sentence
test: «The class chose the pet's name in a democratic vote.» Which word means the same as democratic here? | *Fair | Lonely | Sleepy | Angry
test: «Ancient Athens is called the birthplace of democracy.» What is democracy? | A rule that only one person decides | *A system where people choose their leaders by voting | A kind of sport | A type of building
exam: Which sentence uses democratic correctly? | The dog was democratic and ate my sandwich | The sun is very democratic today | I felt democratic after my lunch | *Our class made a democratic decision to paint the wall blue by a show of hands
